            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Not sure if `runtime/lua/vim/_core/defaults.lua` is the best place to put this but I couldn't find any better place.\r\n\r\nJust ran into a problem with using `defaults.lua`: If you create an additional thread with `uv.new_thread()`, that thread will not have `./?.lua` removed from it. I can move the code to `runtime/lua/vim/_core/shared.lua` to fix this, but that presents another problem: `arg` is never set inside of threads, so there's no way to check if `-l` is being used. This leaves us with three options:\r\n- Don't patch this security issue for threads.\r\n- Don't add `./?.lua` back inside threads while using `-l`. (What I recommend)\r\n- Find some other way to detect `-l` mode that works in all threads.\r\n\r\nEdit: I've pushed an example of doing option 2. It works well, but hopefully it's obvious how it's a little janky.",
            "created_at": "2026-07-16T02:25:14Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40610#issuecomment-4987535930",
            "id": 4987535930,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/40610",
            "minimized": null,
            "node_id": "IC_kwDOAPphoM8AAAABKUfCOg",
            "performed_via_github_app": null,
            "reactions": {
                "+1": 0,
                "-1": 0,
                "confused": 0,
                "eyes": 0,
                "heart": 0,
                "hooray": 0,
